IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgoa-supply`

-- Supply of Goods Act 1982, ss 1-11, 18 and 19(2) -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_supply-of-goods-act-1982.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a contractor's faulty water heater` MEANS Supply WITH
    `it is a hire` IS FALSE
    `the contract transfers only such title as the transferor has` IS FALSE
    `the supplier had no right to transfer` IS FALSE
    `the supplier acts in the course of a business` IS TRUE
    `a business agent supplies for a private owner` IS FALSE
    `the recipient knew or was told the owner was private` IS FALSE
    `the goods are of unsatisfactory quality` IS TRUE
    `the defect was drawn to the recipient's attention before the contract` IS FALSE
    `the recipient examined the goods before the contract` IS FALSE
    `that examination ought to have revealed the defect` IS FALSE
    `the supply was by description` IS FALSE
    `the goods correspond with the description` IS FALSE
    `the supply was by reference to a sample` IS FALSE
    `the bulk corresponds with the sample in quality` IS FALSE
